# Convex folder layout

Read `docs/convex-folder-layout.md` before adding or moving anything under `convex/`.

## Do

- One folder per area. Inside it, only `queries.ts`, `mutations.ts`, and `actions.ts`, and only the kinds that area has.
- Name each folder after an area in this app (`shows`, `discover`, `profile`). A new area uses the same file rules under its own name.
- Call them so the path says the kind: `api.shows.actions.add`.
- Put helpers that are not a query, mutation, or action in `convex/lib/`, named for the area (`discoverPool.ts`, `showModel.ts`).
- Inside a file: values, then types, then private functions, then exports. Synchronous functions before `async` in each group.
- Tests in `__tests__` next to the file, named after it (`queries.test.ts`).
- Leave `schema.ts`, `crons.ts`, `http.ts`, `auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts`, and `testModules.ts` at the `convex/` root.

## Do not

- Mix queries, mutations, and actions in one file.
- Put a helper in a feature folder.
- Add an empty `queries.ts`, `mutations.ts`, or `actions.ts`.
- Name a lib file `helpers.ts` or `utils.ts`.
- Add a test whose only job is to prove `crons.ts` registered a job.
